[CENTER][SIZE=7][B][COLOR=#22b8cf]BlocksAdder[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4]Custom Items • Blocks • Furniture • Crops • Resource Packs[/SIZE]
[B]By Lino | Spigot & Paper | Minecraft Java 1.21.11–26.3[/B]
[URL=https://github.com/lino9999/BlocksAdder/releases]Download[/URL] • [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/BlocksAdder]Source Code[/URL] • [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/BlocksAdder/blob/main/docs/configuration.md]Documentation[/URL][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B]Build your server's custom content[/B][/SIZE]
BlocksAdder lets you define namespaced Minecraft items, decorative blocks, interactive furniture, growing crops, crafting recipes and player HUDs in YAML. Generate a resource pack and bring your content to ordinary Minecraft Java clients.
Development 1.1.0-SNAPSHOT uses the independent [B]blocksadder/bundle-1[/B] typed-record format. Historical 1.0.0 downloads have an older format and a smaller feature set; match the documentation to the installed version.

[SIZE=5][B]What you can create[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Custom items:[/B] modern item models, names and lore, model data, stack sizes, durability, enchantments, attributes, armor colors, food and equipment assets.
[*][B]Custom blocks:[/B] display models with collision, protected placement/removal and persistent chunk data.
[*][B]Furniture:[/B] interaction hitboxes, optional collision and seats.
[*][B]Placed-content actions:[/B] independent use, removal and crop-harvest plans with cancellation and retained delayed-source identity.
[*][B]Held interactions:[/B] shared native routing for both hands, managed furniture/crop helpers and model helpers, with protected cancellation and source-safe consumption.
[*][B]Environmental rules:[/B] protect crops and explosion-sensitive blocks or run effects after committed removal, with delayed source guards and chunk cleanup.
[*][B]Effects and totems:[/B] typed native effects, portable disc playback/stop and custom item activation, with component-preserving displays and authoritative hand restoration.
[*][B]Particle actions:[/B] colored dust, block/item particles, trails and following vibrations, with bounded cloud/line emission settings.
[*][B]Projectile plans:[/B] native launch and block/entity impacts, custom ammunition, offhand use, delayed impact effects and protected projectile damage.
[*][B]Area mining:[/B] bounded native/custom block regions, optional direction and filters, individual protection, tool rules and durability.
[*][B]Conditional world changes:[/B] replace matching native/custom blocks or furnishings through protected transactions, with source checks, rollback and native storage payload retention.
[*][B]Crops:[/B] growth stages, farmland requirements, harvesting, configurable produce and personal distance/detail settings.
[*][B]Nine recipe types:[/B] shaped, shapeless, furnace, blasting, smoking, campfire, stonecutting, smithing and anvil.
[*][B]Player features:[/B] persistent stats, regeneration, bossbar/actionbar HUDs, right-click actions, cooldowns and simple gesture/effect timelines.
[*][B]World features:[/B] configured living mobs, equipment, custom drops, fishing loot and manually generated trees.
[*][B]Fonts and sounds:[/B] bitmap glyphs, permission-aware chat/sign/book aliases, custom audio definitions and sound commands.
[*][B]Resource-pack tools:[/B] modern model generation, asset merging, stable ZIP output and hashes, external hosting or optional built-in HTTP delivery.
[*][B]Administration:[/B] paginated item catalog, recipe previews, per-command permissions, content validation and reload rollback.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Get started[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Install the release JAR in your server's plugins folder and restart.
[*]Review the generated example content and config.yml.
[*]Run [B]/ba validate[/B] and [B]/ba pack build[/B].
[*]Host the generated ZIP, configure resource-pack.url, then run [B]/ba reload[/B].
[*]Use [B]/ba pack send[/B], [B]/ba browse[/B] and [B]/ba get blocksadder:crystal_block[/B].
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Commands at a glance[/B][/SIZE]
[CODE]/ba help
/ba browse [category] [player]
/ba get <item> [amount]
/ba give <player> <item> [amount] [silent]
/ba recipe <item> [player]
/ba inspect
/ba plants <auto|full|hide|status> [player]
/ba validate
/ba reload
/ba pack <build|send|hash> [player|all][/CODE]
The complete command and permission reference is in the documentation tab and [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/BlocksAdder#commands-and-permissions]README[/URL]. Main aliases: [B]/blocksadder[/B], [B]/ba[/B], [B]/badd[/B]. Administration permission: [B]blocksadder.admin[/B].

[SIZE=5][B]Requirements[/B][/SIZE]
Spigot or Paper for Minecraft Java 1.21.11–26.3. Java 21 for 1.21.11; Java 25 for 26.x. No mandatory plugin dependencies. Custom visuals require the generated resource pack. Folia and Bedrock packs are not supported. Exact executed server checks are published in the [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/BlocksAdder/blob/main/docs/verification.md]verification report[/URL].

[SIZE=5][B]Current release scope[/B][/SIZE]
The downloadable 1.0.0 remains an initial preview. Current source additionally implements timed mining, skeletal models, player disguises, controlled vehicles, fluid/fire simulation and bounded generation, with individual acceptance limits. Complete functional reconstruction and dedicated integration coverage remain in progress. Visual checks belong to the user. See [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/BlocksAdder/blob/main/docs/parity-progress.md]current implementation status[/URL] and the [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/BlocksAdder/blob/main/docs/independent-implementation.md]independent distribution audit[/URL].

[B]Open source • English messages • Public Bukkit API • No activation server or telemetry[/B]
Report reproducible issues at [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/BlocksAdder/issues]GitHub Issues[/URL], including server build, Java version, relevant YAML and logs.

[B]Development preview 13 camera compatibility:[/B] fixes the tested Paper 26.3/ProtocolLib movement disconnect. Native camera input and lifecycle pass on nine builds; exact server/protocol scope and remaining visual checks are recorded in the [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/BlocksAdder/blob/main/docs/camera-input.md]camera verification guide[/URL].

[B]Image HUDs and player meters:[/B] Development preview 14 adds full/partial/empty icon bars, quantity frames, custom API-controlled icon sequences, named fonts and pixel positioning. Shared meters retain independent bounds and source-specific bypass, with eligible player timers, world/biome/light rules, food/respawn changes and protected depleted effects. Read the [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/BlocksAdder/blob/main/docs/hud-meters.md]HUD and meter guide[/URL] for the independent bundle schema and exact limits.

[B]Optional PlaceholderAPI exports:[/B] Current development exposes registered glyphs, raw characters, font identifiers, signed pixel spacing and player meter values through the blocksadder expansion. Use canonical namespaced IDs such as %blocksadder_meter_garden:stamina%. Install PlaceholderAPI separately; integrations.placeholders defaults to true. Build and distribute the pack while the adapter is active for generated spacing support. Scalar strings require the consuming plugin to select the configured font. Read the [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/BlocksAdder/blob/main/docs/placeholders.md]complete placeholder guide[/URL] for the five families, asynchronous numeric fallbacks, permissions and provider lifecycle limits.
